"name":"Sol Ring","oracle_id":"6ad8011d-3471-4369-9d68-b264cc027487","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}{C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Enchant"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{G}","name":"Song of the Dryads","oracle_id":"7c3944fa-7c86-4979-85a9-86196aa94594","oracle_text":"Enchant permanent\nEnchanted permanent is a colorless Forest land.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-08-04","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment — Aura"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth","oracle_id":"8dd5f5af-d2d8-4356-8617-8381081b930c","oracle_text":"Each land is a Forest in addition to its other land types.","power":null,"produced_mana":["G"],"released_at":"2021-06-18","toughness":null,"type_line":"Legendary Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature's power and/or toughness, such as the ones created by Titanic Growth or a +1/+1 counter, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch power and toughness.","oracle_id":"02628058-c9d8-4265-afd1-3fb697ec89f7","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the artifact was already a creature, its base power and toughness will each become 5. This overwrites any previous effects that set the creature's base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Ensoul Artifact becomes attached to the artifact will overwrite this effect.","oracle_id":"02628058-c9d8-4265-afd1-3fb697ec89f7","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The artifact retains any types, subtypes, or supertypes it has. Notably, if an Equipment becomes an artifact creature, it usually can't be attached to another creature. If it was attached to a creature, it becomes unattached.","oracle_id":"02628058-c9d8-4265-afd1-3fb697ec89f7","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The resulting artifact creature will be able to attack on your turn if it's been under your control continuously since the turn began. That is, it doesn't matter how long it's been a creature, just how long it's been on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"02628058-c9d8-4265-afd1-3fb697ec89f7","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The owner of a copy of a spell is the player under whose control it was put onto the stack.","oracle_id":"060ef981-db05-436b-b1c1-f55071375344","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The player who creates a token is its owner.","oracle_id":"060ef981-db05-436b-b1c1-f55071375344","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you are unable to cast the card (there are no legal targets for the spell, for example), nothing happens when Memory Plunder resolves, and the card remains in its owner's graveyard.","oracle_id":"36b67014-0507-4976-ad52-a2a36676197d","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast a card “without paying its mana cost,” you can't pay any alternative costs. On the other hand, if the card has additional costs (such as conspire), you may pay those.","oracle_id":"36b67014-0507-4976-ad52-a2a36676197d","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you want to cast the card, you cast it as part of the resolution of Memory Plunder. Timing restrictions based on the card's type are ignored if it's a sorcery. Other casting restrictions are not (such as “Cast [this card] only during combat”).","oracle_id":"36b67014-0507-4976-ad52-a2a36676197d","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn’t cause you gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"5912546a-acc2-448c-b042-64bdac5ec129","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the permanent was an Aura or an Equipment, it becomes unattached from whatever it was attached to.","oracle_id":"7c3944fa-7c86-4979-85a9-86196aa94594","published_at":"2014-11-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The enchanted permanent loses any card types, subtypes, and colors it previously had. It keeps any supertypes it had and its name remains unchanged. It gains “{T}: Add {G}” and loses all other abilities from its rules text. It will still have any abilities it gained from other effects.","oracle_id":"7c3944fa-7c86-4979-85a9-86196aa94594","published_at":"2014-11-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Land cards not on the battlefield aren't Forests while Yavimaya is on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"8dd5f5af-d2d8-4356-8617-8381081b930c","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Yavimaya's ability causes each land on the battlefield to have the land type Forest. Any land that's a Forest has the ability \"{T}: Add {G}.\" Nothing else changes about those lands, including their names, other subtypes, and whether they're legendary, basic, or snow.","oracle_id":"8dd5f5af-d2d8-4356-8617-8381081b930c","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth isn't a Forest while it's not on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"8dd5f5af-d2d8-4356-8617-8381081b930c","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn't matter how long the permanent has been a creature.","oracle_id":"8f0179fe-6d7d-49cc-ab06-d3b402c6fc8d","published_at":"2008-08-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a permanent doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of an Aura or Equipment doesn't change what it's attached to.","oracle_id":"d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a permanent doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of an Aura or Equipment doesn't change what it's attached to.","oracle_id":"d599a38c-7719-443e-bb59-55bd43a8fee6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
